  "id": "social-dominance-theory",
  "term": "social dominance theory",
  "definition": "Social dominance theory is a social framework for understanding intergroup relations that emphasizes how group-based hierarchies shape people’s behavior. In this view, unequal positions between groups help organize social interactions and outcomes.",
